  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary:\nLoading a malformed note file in the Evernote(Windows) application will cause XSS in the application, leading to an RCE\n\n## Steps To Reproduce:\n\n### STEP[Creation of malormed note file]\n  1. Install Evernote's Web Clip extension(https://evernote.com/intl/jp/features/webclipper) in my browser and execute \"Clip Full Page\" on any website.  \ninfo: I installed this on Google Chrome.\n  2. Open the installed Evernote application and open the note of the clipped web page.\n  3. Export note in ENEX format.  \n  {F2623333}\n  4. In the exported ENEX file, insert the HTML-entityized XSS payload in the \"--en-clipped-source-title\" section. And save the file.  \ninfo: In XPath, it is the style attribute \"--en-clipped-source-title\" of the div element in the CDATA that can be obtained by \"/en-export/note/content/text()\".\n\nI have inserted this payload.\n```\n&quot;&gt;&lt;img src onerror=eval(atob(&apos;&apos;))&gt;\n```\n\nThe malformed note file is here.\n{F2623355}\n\n### STEP[Load malformed note file cause XSS and RCE]\n  1. Open the installed Evernote application and import the malformed note file.\n  2. A few seconds after the import is complete, the Windows calculator application will launch.\n  {F2623357}\n\nNOTE:\nEvernote versions is \n10.60.4-win-winstore-public (20230803182206)\nThis is the latest version available for installation from the Microsoft Store as of August 22, 2023 (JST).\n\n\n## How It works:\nThe following code is executed in the XSS that occurs when the note file import completes.\n```\nsetTimeout(()=>{window.electronApi.ipcRenderer.send(\"BrokerBridge\",{action:\"Bridge/Publish\",topics:\"boron.actions.openBrowserWindow\",type:\"\",data:{\"requiresAuthentication\":false,\"url\":\"file:///C:/Windows/System32/calc.exe\"}});},5000);\n```\nIn this code, the following steps are taken:\n1. Wait 5 seconds\n2. Using the \"window.electronApi.ipcRenderer.send\" prepared in Preload, the \"BrokerBridge\" function is called in the main process via IPC communication.\n3. \"boron.actions.openBrowserWindow\" function could be used to run local applications.\n\n## Impact\n\nLoading an malformed note file in an application can result in command execution, program execution, or access to an external URL.",
